target/m68k: EMAC saturation clamps at 32 bits, and latches

MCF54455RM Table 5-2: with OMC set, a signed or fractional accumulator overflow
is judged and clamped at the SIGNED 32-BIT boundary (the fractional accumulator
carries its 1.31 value at bits 39:8), not at the 48-bit accumulator width — and
saturation LATCHES: while PAVn is set the accumulator ignores further MAC/MSAC
until the flag is cleared or the accumulator is loaded directly.

QEMU accumulated in TCG and saturated afterwards at 48 bits, so a
saturating-mode overflow wrapped instead of clamping, and never froze. Move the
accumulate into a helper that freezes on PAVn and clamps at the 32-bit bounds.
Audibly wrong for DSP code under MACSR = fractional + saturating: wrapped
negative accumulations turn the negative half of a waveform into zeros and its
zero crossings into full-scale bursts.

